WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.150
Plan the day backwards, hand over a safe room, and keep records.

2
00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:08.870
This is the video for module three of Event Decoration and Styling.

3
00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:14.860
On the event day, guests arrive when the invitation says, not when you finish.

4
00:00:16.110 --> 00:00:20.840
So good decorators plan the day backwards, from the moment the room must be ready.

5
00:00:22.090 --> 00:00:29.390
Your name is attached to every piece you install. A safe room and honest dealing are part of quality, not extras.

6
00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:37.340
And each event is a lesson you have already paid for. Without records, the lesson disappears after the weekend.

7
00:00:38.590 --> 00:00:47.570
Step one. Set your ready time, at least 30 to 60 minutes before guests are expected. Photographers and the client will arrive early.

8
00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:52.980
Step two. List every task, with a time from your practice sessions.

9
00:00:54.230 --> 00:01:02.020
Step three. Decide which tasks run at the same time, with different helpers. Give each helper a photo of the finished zone.

10
00:01:03.270 --> 00:01:10.650
Step four. Add a buffer of about 20 to 25 percent for late deliveries, a locked hall, or a missing item.

11
00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:19.810
Step five. Add loading and travel time, allowing for Saturday morning traffic. That gives you the time you must leave home.

12
00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:30.320
For example, Grace's church reception starts at 12 noon, with guests from 11:30. She sets her ready time at 11:00.

13
00:01:31.570 --> 00:01:37.950
From 7:30, she and one helper build the backdrop, while two helpers do tables and chair covers.

14
00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:41.310
Then centrepieces and the entrance.

15
00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:45.570
A 30 minute buffer, then a 15 minute walkthrough.

16
00:01:46.820 --> 00:01:59.680
She arrives at 7:00 to unload and sort by zone. With 45 minutes of Saturday traffic, she leaves home by 6:15. Pack crates by zone, and tick them in and out.

17
00:02:00.930 --> 00:02:14.610
Real candles can set fabric, flowers or hair on fire. Keep them at least 12 inches, about 30 cm, from anything that burns, or use flameless candles. LED lights run cooler next to fabric.

18
00:02:15.860 --> 00:02:24.070
Use one extension box per wall socket, and never plug one box into another. Route cables along walls and tape them flat.

19
00:02:25.320 --> 00:02:41.850
Weight every stand and tie arches to fixed points, especially outdoors in wind. Generators make carbon monoxide, so they run outside, away from doors, windows and canopies. At children's parties, pick up burst balloon pieces at once.

20
00:02:43.100 --> 00:02:56.050
Before guests arrive, walk the room. Does it match what the client approved? Is it secure? Give each piece a gentle shake. Are walkways and exits clear? Is it neat, with no visible tape? And is it clean?

21
00:02:56.400 --> 00:03:02.570
Then photograph every zone while the room is empty. Those are your portfolio pictures, and your proof.

22
00:03:03.820 --> 00:03:19.780
For example, Amaka in Abuja found the hotel's ceiling hooks removed. She dropped the ceiling drape, moved the fabric to two extra backdrop frames, called the agreed contact, and offered a partial refund. Tell clients early, and agree in writing.

23
00:03:21.030 --> 00:03:31.560
A silent substitution damages trust more than the change itself. Never improvise fixings from light fittings. And only post photos of work you actually did.

24
00:03:32.810 --> 00:03:43.400
Keep one row per job: quoted price and actual costs, planned and actual setup time, client rating out of 5, referrals, and anything damaged or lost.

25
00:03:44.650 --> 00:03:56.340
For example, Tolu reviewed three birthday jobs. On one, she quoted 282,000 naira, spent 214,000, and made 68,000 profit.

26
00:03:57.590 --> 00:04:02.490
Every setup ran 15 to 20 percent over plan, mostly on balloon garlands.

27
00:04:03.740 --> 00:04:10.630
On another job, flower prices rose after she quoted, and with no validity date, it came out of her profit.

28
00:04:11.880 --> 00:04:19.540
So she adds 20 percent to garland time, builds garlands the night before, and writes valid for 7 days on every quote.

29
00:04:20.790 --> 00:04:36.840
To remember. Plan backwards from the ready time, with a buffer. Control flames, cables, stands and generators. Walk through and photograph before guests arrive. Tell clients about changes early. And keep a job record you review every month.

30
00:04:38.090 --> 00:04:45.890
Now write your event-day run sheet with a leave-home time, do a hazard check of a hall you might decorate, and start your job record.

31
00:04:46.240 --> 00:04:48.180
Continue with the lessons below.
